  "pages": 1
 },
 "summary": "A male pin header on a 1.27 mm grid with two rows of 0.4 mm square brass pins standing straight up from a 1.0 mm thick insulating strip. Below the strip each pin bends outward into a flat gull-wing foot, so the two rows solder to pads on either side of the body. Pins are gold or tin over nickel; rated 1.0 A, 500 V AC/DC withstand, -40 to +105 °C. PZ127-2-07-S has 7 pins per row, 14 positions, without locating posts.",
